= Glossary

/ Accuracy: (1) Fact of being exact or correct. (2) Proportion of all choices that were correct or optimal.

/ Belief: Internal representation, held by an agent, that a proposition or percept corresponds to the actual state of the world.

/ Bias: Systematic tendency of a decision-maker to favor one alternative over the others.

/ Calibration: TODO

/ Choice: Alternative (option) selected by a decision.

/ Confidence: Subjective, graded estimate of how likely a belief, valuation, decision, or action is to be correct, accurate, or successful.

/ Decision: Deliberative process resulting in the commitment to one alternative over others.

/ Decision-making: Process by which sensory information, internal states, and learned experiences are integrated to generate behavioral choices.

/ Metacognition: TODO

/ Metacognitive bias: TODO

/ Metacognitive efficiency: TODO

/ Metacognitive sensitivity: TODO

/ Sensitivity: Ability of a decision-maker to distinguish signal (useful information) from noise.

/ Uncertainty: Variability in the representation of information during a decision.

/ Value: Subjective worth or desirability of an outcome.

/ Trust: Willingness to rely on another person, system, or source despite uncertainty.
